            <ArticleTitle>Twenty-four hour plasma profile of sustained-release isosorbide mononitrate in healthy volunteers and in patients with chronic stable angina. Two open label trials.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>333-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIMS" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">The plasma profile of a single dose of isosorbide mononitrate 25 mg (Elantan LA25) in healthy volunteers and in angina patients was examined.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">In volunteers and patients, blood samples for pharmacokinetics were obtained pre-dosing and at intervals for 24 h after dosing.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">This formulation exhibited rapid absorption and plasma levels were maintained at &gt; 100 ng ml-1 for up to 9 to 12 h.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">A comparison of the pharmacokinetics of Elantan LA25 in volunteers and patients indicates that the profiles are similar.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
